# The hemp shirt and harem pants on a baby zombie, husk, drowned, zombie villager or piglin: the
# equipment asset's humanoid_baby layer (equipment/hemp_fiber.json), one 64x64 texture for every
# slot, laid out for vanilla's baby armour model (HumanoidModel#createBabyArmorMesh). Placeholder
# art drawn from the grown-up textures' own greys. Render with mctex.py render into
# common/src/main/resources/assets/hempdustry/textures.

@palette default
. = none
E = FFFFFF        shirt: highlight
D = E8E8E8        shirt: light
I = DEDEDE        shirt: light, weave
B = BEBEBE        shirt: base
G = CCCCCC        shirt: mid
N = B7B7B7        shirt: hem
C = B0B0B0        shirt: shadow
h = D4D4D4        pants: light
d = C6C6C6        pants: mid, light
g = C1C1C1        pants: mid
a = 9C9C9C        pants: base
b = 919191        pants: shadow
f = 878787        pants: gathered cuff

@palette overlay
. = none
k = 352623        shirt button
s = 0F0F0D        drawstring

# Grey, tinted by the dye or by the undyed colour, as the grown-up hemp_fiber_dyeable is. Each face
# row starts at the model's UV; spaces in the notes below mark the faces (side, front, side, back).
#   shirt body   (0,17) 6x5x3: faces rows 20-24, x 0-2 3-8 9-11 12-17; the V-neck at the front's top
#   sleeves      (30,17) and (30,25) 2x5x3: faces rows 20-22 and 28-30, x 30-32 33-34 35-37 38-39;
#                the shoulders on the tops, x 33-34 rows 17-19 and 25-27. Three of five rows, as
#                vanilla's leather sleeves are.
#   trouser legs (18,17) and (18,24) 3x4x3: faces rows 20-22 and 27-29, x 18-20 21-23 24-26 27-29,
#                gathered at the bottom row; the feet stay bare for the flip-flops.
#   waistband    (0,36) 5.9x2x2.9: faces rows 39-40 (row 38 shows a tenth of a pixel), x 0-17.
@texture entity/equipment/humanoid_baby/hemp_fiber_dyeable 64x64
